parameter policy, marginal on one qubit; theta = 0.05
  ref 0.50 (original-centred reference (the study's universe)): original passes, mutant passes
  ref 0.46 (off-centre reference admitted by the QUTest grammar): original passes, mutant fails
  study difference d = 0.02 <= theta, so the study's universe holds no distinguishing instance

distance conventions at support-zero and small-probability boundaries
  mutant has support where the original has none: TV 0.01, Hellinger 0.0709, KL(M||P) 0.22, |dH| 0.0707  (QUTest and study agree)
  original has support where the mutant has none: TV 0.01, Hellinger 0.0709, KL(M||P) 0.0101, |dH| 0.0707  (QUTest and study agree)
  difference at the 1e-10 equality margin: TV 1e-10, Hellinger 7.07e-06, KL(M||P) 9.54e-11, |dH| 3.37e-09  (QUTest and study agree)
  KL direction: QUTest computes D(measured || reference); the study computes D(p_M || p_P), the same direction.
  A KL instance is not symmetric: D(p_P || p_M) would differ, but no admitted instance uses that direction.
